11:34:36 AM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 53438ms :: {"response":"Okay, here’s a sample weight loss diet plan tailored for you, Mani. Remember that individual results may vary depending on lifestyle factors like exercise habits and overall calorie expenditure. It's always best to consult with a registered dietitian or healthcare professional for personalized guidance. Also note I am unable to provide exact caloric values due to lack of information about activity level etc. These numbers will need to be adjusted accordingly by consulting a dietician.\n\n## 🌅 Breakfast\n*   **Oats Porridge:** ½ cup rolled oats cooked with skim milk OR water, topped with ¼ cup berries and a sprinkle of chia seeds (~200 Calories)\n*   **Egg White Scramble:** 3 Egg Whites scrambled with chopped onions, peppers, and spinach (~150 Calories)\n\n## 🍎 Mid-Morning Snack\n*   **Apple Slices with Almond Butter:** 1 medium apple sliced with 1 tablespoon almond butter (~200 Calories)\n\n## 🍽️ Lunch\n*   **Chicken Salad Sandwich (Whole Wheat):** Chicken salad made from grilled chicken breast mixed with Greek yogurt instead of mayo, served on two slices of whole wheat bread with lettuce and tomato (~350 Calories)\n*   **Small Side Salad:** Mixed green salad with cucumber, carrots, and light vinaigrette dressing (~100 Calories)\n\n## 🌆 Evening Snack\n*   **Greek Yogurt with Berries:** Plain non fat greek yoghurt with half cup of mixed berries (~150 Calories)\n\n## 🌙 Dinner\n*   **Vegetable Curry with Brown Rice:** A portion of vegetable curry prepared without added oils using brown rice ~300 Calories\n\n## ⚠️ Foods to Avoid\n*   Processed snacks (chips, cookies, pastries)\n*   Sugary drinks (soda, juice)\n*   Fried foods\n*   Excessive amounts of cheese and creamy sauces\n\n## 💡 Why This Plan\n*   **Weight Loss Focus**: The primary focus is reducing calorie intake through lean protein sources, high fiber options, and mindful portion control.\n*   **Protein Intake**: High protein helps preserve muscle mass during weight loss while promoting satiety.\n*   **Fiber Content**: Fiber promotes fullness which can aid in appetite management.\n*   **Healthy Fats**: Incorporating healthy unsaturated fats supports hormone production and nutrient absorption.\n*   **Hydration**: Drinking plenty of water throughout the day aids digestion and metabolism.\n\n[MACROS: Protein 45%, Carbs 35%, Fat 20%]","followUpQuestions":[]}
