11:37:47 AM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 55605ms :: {"response":"Here's an Indian Diet Plan for Fat Loss:\n\n## 🌅 Breakfast\n*   **Poha:** 1 cup Poha (flattened rice) prepared with minimal oil and spices, garnished with coriander leaves (~250 Calories)\n*   **Sprouts Salad:** Mix sprouts(moong, chana) with lemon juice, onion ,carrot and pepper(~150 Calories)\n\n## 🍎 Mid-Morning Snack\n*   **Roasted Chana Chaat:** 1 cup roasted chickpeas seasoned with chaat masala and lime (~180 Calories)\n\n## 🍽️ Lunch\n*   **Dal Makhani (small Portion):** Small serving of Dal Makhani (black lentil dish) - approximately ¾ cup (~300 Calories)\n*   **Brown Rice:** 1 cup boiled brown rice (~200 Calories)\n*   **Mixed Vegetable Sabzi:** 1 cup mixed seasonal vegetables stir-fried with very little oil (~150 Calories)\n\n## 🌆 Evening Snack\n*   **Cucumber Raita:** Cucumber raita made with plain yogurt and herbs (~100 Calories)\n\n## 🌙 Dinner\n*   **Methi Paratha:** 1 Methi paratha (fenugreek leaf stuffed flatbread) – Wholewheat flour base (~250 Calories)\n*   **Salad:** Simple salad with lettuce and some veggies (~100 Calories)\n\n## ⚠️ Foods to Avoid\n*   Deep Fried Snacks (Pakoras, samosa)\n*   Creamy Curd Based Dishes (Butter Milk dishes )\n*   Sugar Rich Desserts (Gulab Jamun, Jalebi)\n*   Excess Oil Usage During Cooking\n\n## 💡 Why This Plan\n*   **Reduced Calorie Density:** Emphasizes meals rich in nutrients relative to their calorie content.\n*   **High Fiber:** Includes lentils, dals, sprouted beans, and whole grains providing sustained energy and aiding in digestion.\n*   **Lean Proteins:** Opting for less oily preparations of pulses and incorporating smaller servings of paneer or tofu ensures sufficient protein intake crucial for preserving muscles during weight reduction.\n*   **Limited Refined Carbohydrates:** Reducing consumption of white rice and opting for brown rice provides more complex carbohydrates leading to slower glucose release thus helping manage hunger pangs better .\n*   **Mindful Portions:** Controlling portion sizes prevents overeating even with healthier choices.\n\n[MACROS: Protein 40%, Carbs 30%, Fat 30%]","followUpQuestions":[]}
