11:56:30 AM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 93394ms :: {"response":"Alright, here's a revised diet plan incorporating your preferred supplements and aiming to mitigate mental fatigue associated with your demanding startup career. Keep in mind this requires careful monitoring and adjustment guided by your own experiences and feedback.\n\n## 🌅 Breakfast (Around 7 AM)\n*   **Overnight Oats:** Combine 1/2 cup rolled oats, 1 scoop whey protein isolate (or plant-based alternative), 1 tbsp chia seeds, 1 cup unsweetened almond milk, and a handful of blueberries in a jar. Refrigerate overnight. Consume upon waking. (*Approximate Calories: 350*)\n    *   *Rationale:* Provides slow-release carbohydrate fuel, protein for satiety, and antioxidants for cellular protection. Overnight preparation saves time. Whey protein offers amino acids critical for neurotransmitter synthesis.\n*   **Coffee (Black or Lightly Brewed):** One cup brewed coffee. (*Approximate Calories: Negligible*)\n    *   *Rationale:* Caffeine stimulates wakefulness and focus. Choose decaf later in the day to prevent nighttime disruption.\n\n## 🍎 Mid-Morning Snack (Around 10 AM)\n*   **Handful of Nuts & Seeds:** Approximately 1/4 cup mixed almonds, pumpkin seeds, and sunflower seeds. (*Approximate Calories: 200*)\n    *   *Rationale:* Healthy fats contribute to brain function, and the combination delivers diverse micronutrients.\n\n## 🍽️ Lunch (Around 1 PM)\n*   **Large Salad Bowl:** Base consisting of 2 cups mixed greens, 4 oz Grilled Salmon or Tofu, 1/2 cup quinoa, assorted colorful vegetables (cucumber, bell peppers, cherry tomatoes), and a light vinaigrette dressing. (*Approximate Calories: 500*)\n    *   *Rationale:* Lean protein fuels the body, complex carbohydrates sustain energy, and abundant produce supplies vitamins and minerals. Quinoa adds extra protein and fiber.\n*   **Water Bottle:** Carry a large refillable bottle filled with water throughout the day.\n\n## 🌆 Afternoon Snack (Around 4 PM)\n*   **Hard Boiled Eggs:** Two hard-boiled eggs. (*Approximate Calories: 160*)\n    *   *Rationale:* Excellent source of choline, a precursor to acetylcholine involved in memory and learning.\n*   **Green Tea:** One cup of Green tea. (*Approximate Calories: Negligible*)\n    *   *Rationale:* Contains caffeine and L-Theanine, offering calm stimulation along with enhanced focus.\n\n## 🌙 Dinner (Around 8 PM)\n*   **Baked Sweet Potato:** Medium sized baked sweet potato drizzled with 1 tsp Coconut Oil and sprinkled with Cinnamon. Serve with steamed broccoli florets. (*Approximate Calories: 350*)\n    *   *Rationale:* Offers complex carbohydrates for steady energy release, beta carotene benefits eye health, and fiber regulates blood sugar. Broccoli provides cruciferous vegetables with detoxifying properties.\n*   **Glass of Warm Milk:** Optional glass of warm milk (dairy or plant-based) before bed. (*Approximate Calories: Negligible*)\n    *   *Rationale:* Can induce relaxation and prepare for restful sleep.\n\n## ⚠️ Foods to Avoid\n*   Highly Processed Foods: Fast Food, packaged snacks, canned goods, frozen dinners.\n*   Added Sugars: Soda, candy, desserts, sweetened juices.\n*   Refined Grains: White Bread, pasta, pastries.\n*   Excess Alcohol: Especially close to bedtime.\n\n## 💊 Supplements Schedule:\n*   **Whey Protein Isolate:** Post Workout Meal *(Post workout)*\n*   **Ashwagandha:** Before Bedtime *(Evening)*\n*   **Rhodiola Rosea:** With Lunch *(Mid afternoon)*\n*   **B-Complex:** Morning *(","followUpQuestions":[]}
