12:06:44 PM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 46967ms :: {"response":"For sautéing, roasting, baking, and generally cooking most things in this diet, **Extra Virgin Olive Oil (EVOO)** is highly recommended. Its monounsaturated fats are heart-healthy and impart flavor.\n\nHowever, keep these points in mind:\n\n*   **Temperature Sensitivity:** EVOO starts breaking down at relatively low temperatures (around 350°F/175°C). So, don't overheat it. Once it smokes, discard it.\n*   **Consider Alternatives:** When heating to extremely high temps (frying, searing steaks), choose something with a higher smoke point, such as Avocado Oil, Sunflower Oil, or Peanut Oil.\n*   **Use Sparingly:** Even healthy oils contain calories. Measure carefully to stay within your target range.\n*   **Flavor Preference:** Taste matters! Feel free to experiment with different types of olive oil (light vs. robust) to suit your preference.\n\nSo, stick primarily to Extra Virgin Olive Oil whenever possible, but know when to switch to alternatives for certain cooking methods.","followUpQuestions":[]}
