12:14:05 PM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 51821ms :: {"response":"Okay, calculating the calorie count for two slices of Domino's Pizza is tricky because ingredients and toppings vary widely. We'll estimate conservatively assuming average slice sizing and commonly available toppings. Note that this calculation assumes a single serving of pizza equals 2 slices.\n\nAssuming a standard 14 inch pizza cut into 8 slices, two slices equate to roughly 1/4 of the entire pie. Let us look at the nutritional facts for a single slice of dominoes pizza :\n\nOne Slice (approx. 1/8th of a 14” pizza):\n\nCalories: Around 250-300 kcal\nProtein: About 8-10g\nFat: About 12-15g\nCarbohydrates: About 25-30g\n\nTwo slices = approx. 500-600kcal total\n\nNow, accounting for topping differences, lets say pepperoni, mushroom, olives, ham...etc.:\n\nTo account for the fact that you are having 2 slices, please remember to factor in double the amount listed previously.\n\nPlease note again that this is still an estimation. Actual values may differ slightly.\n\n[MACROS: Protein 30%, Carbs 40%, Fat 30%]","followUpQuestions":[]}
