12:44:34 PM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 47056ms :: {"response":"Vodka is predominantly ethanol (alcohol), meaning it doesn't contain substantial amounts of protein, carbohydrates, or fat.\n\nEstimates for 60ml of vodka (approximately 2 ounces):\n\n*   **Calories:** Very few, perhaps 60-70 kcal.\n*   **Protein:** Almost negligible, maybe <1g.\n*   **Carbohydrates:** Virtually zero (<1g).\n*   **Fat:** Essentially zero.\n\nKeep in mind that drinking too much alcohol can lead to dehydration and negatively impact your overall health. Moderation is key.","followUpQuestions":[]}
[MedGemma] Sending message with session diet-planner_1
[MedGemma] Response received: You raise a valid point. The 70 kcal figure repres... | Follow-ups: 0
12:49:34 PM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 48273ms :: {"response":"You raise a valid point. The 70 kcal figure represents the energy contained within the chemical bonds holding the molecules together in the liquid form of pure ethanol (which makes up almost all of vodka). That energy comes from the carbon atoms originally derived from fermented materials like grain or grapes. Think of it like burning wood – the heat released is essentially stored energy waiting to be unlocked chemically.\n\nEssentially, the human body breaks down the ethanol molecule to extract usable energy, releasing that energy in the process. The 70 kcal reflects the net energy gained by the body from metabolizing the alcohol consumed.","followUpQuestions":[]}
